<title>BELGIUM: Belgium cuts liquidity at money tender.</title>
<headline>Belgium cuts liquidity at money tender.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian central bank cut liquidity at its fixed-rate tender for seven-day advances.</p>
<p>Details -</p>
<p>    Value date 05/02	  expiry on 12/02    NBVA</p>
<p>    Amount allotted	    9.975 bln bfr    (15.500 bln *)</p>
<p>    Interest rate		3.00 pct	    (3.00 pct **)</p>
<p>    Total amount of bids    27.000 bln bfr</p>
<p>Percentage of bids accepted  36.66 pct</p>
<p>* amount draining from the money market on February 5</p>
<p>** interest rate at previous tender on January 27</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
